[00:00.94]Lesson 33 | 第33课
[00:03.04]Education | 教育
[00:10.92]Why is education democratic in bookless tribal societies? | 为什么在没有文字的部落社会中教育是民主的？
[00:18.65]Education is one of the key words of our time. | 教育是我们这个时代的关键词之一。
[00:23.29]A man without an education, many of us believe, | 我们许多人相信，一个没有受过教育的人，
[00:27.40]is an unfortunate victim of adverse circumstances, deprived of one of the greatest twentieth-century opportunities. | 是逆境的不幸牺牲品，被剥夺了20世纪最伟大的机遇之一。
[00:37.15]Convinced of the importance of education, modern states 'invest' in institutions of learning to get back 'interest' | 由于深信教育的重要性，现代国家“投资”于教育机构，以期收回“利息”，
[00:46.84]in the form of a large group of enlightened young men and women who are potential leaders. | 这种利息以一大群有见识的青年男女的形式出现，他们是潜在的领袖。
[00:53.93]Education, with its cycles of instruction so carefully worked out, | 教育，以其精心安排的教学循环，
[00:59.35]punctuated by textbooks--those purchasable wells of wisdom--what would civilization be like without its benefits? | 以教科书——那些可以买到的智慧之井——为标志，倘若没有教育的种种好处，文明将会是什么样子？
[01:10.77]So much is certain: that we would have doctors and preachers, | 至少有一点是肯定的：我们仍会有医生和牧师、
[01:16.51]lawyers and defendants marriages and births--but our spiritual outlook would be different. | 律师和被告、婚姻和生育——但我们的精神面貌会不同。
[01:25.07]We would lay less stress on 'facts and figures' and more on a good memory, | 我们会更少强调“事实和数据”，而更多强调好的记忆力，
[01:31.53]on applied psychology, and on the capacity of a man to get along with his fellow-citizens. | 强调应用心理学，以及一个人与同胞相处的能力。
[01:39.04]If our educational system were fashioned after its bookless past we would have the most democratic form of 'college' imaginable. | 如果我们的教育制度是仿照没有书本的过去塑造的，我们就将拥有可以想像得到的最民主的“学院”形式。
[01:50.08]Among tribal people all knowledge inherited by tradition is shared by all; | 在部落人群中，所有由传统继承下来的知识为大家所共享；
[01:56.92]it is taught to every member of the tribe so that in this respect everybody is equally equipped for life. | 这些知识传授给部落的每一个成员，因此在这方面人人都为生活做好了同等的准备。
[02:06.45]It is the ideal condition of the 'equal start' which only our most progressive forms of modern education try to regain. | 这正是“平等起点”的理想状态，只有我们最先进的现代教育形式才试图重获这种状态。
[02:17.00]In primitive cultures the obligation to seek and to receive the traditional instruction is binding to all. | 在原始文化中，寻求和接受传统教育的义务对所有人都有约束力。
[02:25.63]There are no'illiterates' --if the term can be applied to peoples without a script--while our own compulsory school attendance became law in Germany in 1642, | 那里没有“文盲”——如果这个词可以用于没有文字的民族的话——而我们的义务学校教育1642年才在德国成为法律，
[02:39.77]in France in 1806, and in England in 1876 and is still nonexistent in a number of 'civilized' nations. | 1806年在法国、1876年在英国成为法律，而且在一些“文明”国家至今仍不存在。
[02:51.14]This shows how long it was before we deemed it necessary to make sure | 这表明，我们经过了多么漫长的时间才认为有必要确保
[02:56.66]that all our children could share in the knowledge accumulated by the 'happy few' during the past centuries. | 我们所有的孩子都能分享“幸运的少数人”在过去若干世纪中积累起来的知识。
[03:07.21]Education in the wilderness is not a matter of monetary means. | 荒野中的教育不是金钱问题。
[03:12.73]All are entitled to an equal start. | 人人都有权获得平等的起点。
[03:16.37]There is none of the hurry which, in our society, often hampers the full development of a growing personality. | 那里没有我们社会中常常阻碍成长中人格充分发展的那种匆忙。
[03:26.13]There, a child grows up under the everpresent attention of his parents; | 在那里，孩子在父母无微不至的关怀下成长；
[03:32.11]therefore the jungles and the savannahs know of no 'juvenile delinquency'. | 因此丛林和热带草原不知道什么叫“少年犯罪”。
[03:39.36]No necessity of making a living away from home results in neglect of children, and no father is confronted with his inability to 'buy' an education for his child. | 没有离家谋生的必要导致对孩子的忽视，也没有哪位父亲会面临无法为孩子“购买”教育的无能为力。
